{%- comment -%}
  Returns the CSS value for the --swatch custom property, following the
  unified swatch priority order (highest to lowest):
    1. Metaobject color (settings.theme_color)
    2. Native Shopify swatch (value.swatch.image / .color)
    3. settings.swatch_color_list textarea  ┐ resolved via CSS
    4. swatches.css hardcoded colors     ┘ variable cascade

  Sources 1 and 2 are resolved here to actual inline values (hex string or
  url()), completely bypassing the CSS variable layer. This means the CSS
  cascade ordering between swatches.css and the inline <style> from
  swatch-color-list.liquid is irrelevant for those two sources.

  Sources 3 and 4 are still resolved via var(--handle). Both live inside
  the .swatches selector and swatch-color-list.liquid writes the textarea
  values before the metaobject values, so within that layer textarea still
  overrides swatches.css.

  Accepts:
  - value: {ProductOptionValueDrop} the option value (must respond to
    `| handle` and may have a `.swatch` SwatchDrop)
  - metaobject_entries: {Array} the metaobjects[settings.theme_color].values
    array, pre-filtered with `| where: 'name'`. Pass nil or empty when
    swatches are disabled or no metaobject is configured; the snippet still
    works but priority 1 is skipped.
  - image_width: {Integer} requested image width for the CDN URL. Defaults
    to 96. The same width is used for both metaobject images and native
    swatch images.

  Output: a CSS value ready to embed in style="--swatch: <output>;", e.g.
    #000000
    url(https://cdn.shopify.com/…/black-swatch.jpg?width=96)
    var(--navy)

  Usage (capture once, strip whitespace):
    {%- capture swatch_value -%}
      {%- render 'swatch-style-value',
            value: value,
            metaobject_entries: metaobject_color_entries,
            image_width: 48
      -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign swatch_value = swatch_value | strip -%}
    style="--swatch: {{ swatch_value }};"
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign image_width = image_width | default: 96
  assign value_handle = value | handle

  assign mo_hex = null
  assign mo_image_url = null

  for entry in metaobject_entries
    assign entry_handle = entry.name | handle
    if entry_handle == value_handle
      if entry.image != blank
        assign mo_image_url = entry.image | image_url: width: image_width
      endif
      if entry.hex_code != blank
        assign mo_hex = entry.hex_code
      endif
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  Priority 1 — metaobject (image beats hex within the same entry, matching
  the behaviour of swatch-color-list.liquid which writes image last).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if mo_image_url != null -%}
  url({{ mo_image_url }})
{%- elsif mo_hex != null -%}
  {{ mo_hex }}
  {%- comment -%}
    Priority 2 — native Shopify swatch (image beats color within the same value).
    value.swatch.color is a hex string (e.g. #40e0d0) — output it directly.
  {%- endcomment -%}
{%- elsif value.swatch.image -%}
  url({{ value.swatch.image | image_url: width: image_width }})
{%- elsif value.swatch.color -%}
  {{ value.swatch.color }}
  {%- comment -%}
    Priority 3/4 — CSS variable fallback (textarea > swatches.css, enforced by
    the cascade inside swatch-color-list.liquid).
  {%- endcomment -%}
{%- else -%}
  var(--{{ value_handle }})
{%- endif -%}
